<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Two rebellious icons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ea2179d9227ceb49dfe951b7cfefd7144752052d35f13d6148684b0fec37bb9</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-two-rebellious-icons/a-79296944--835a4e14c380.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-two-rebellious-icons/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece — a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan suicide bombing targets police facility in Kohat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbf7916424da87c2e6ee3c93f72b4e8b4c3d20d9b1189865a22379fa76c4d1d0</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432--8b09a06dd711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A police official said the explosion killed at least 16 people, injuring many more. The attacker targeted a police facility and damaged a mosque at the site. The president blamed the attack on the TTP Pakistani Taliban</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8baf976eff7145b3e5ad9cb870949704258aa7c68713a5d4aea2b31804202315</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz is facing record low approval ratings which embolden his opponents. How can a chancellor be removed from office in Germany? There are three options.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The rise of the AfD: The all-or-nothing party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b77c4bfebbbae98876cb96886f150a95d7c385441bc312477369f02689c815c7</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-rise-of-the-afd-the-all-or-nothing-party/a-79326208--4fd4b9219f1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-rise-of-the-afd-the-all-or-nothing-party/a-79326208?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD is riding high after its latest electoral triumph in Saxony-Anhalt. But one question remains: Does the far-right party actually want to govern?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: At least 3 students killed in school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40586684a2fd501bceee3a35800bc1e1f75e96d4e5691f50ddda2f2170fee8db</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-at-least-3-students-killed-in-school-shooting/a-79319854--78d522a17cea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-at-least-3-students-killed-in-school-shooting/a-79319854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emergency services received reports of gunfire at the Banga National High School in southern Mindanao on Friday afternoon. At least three students were killed, including the suspected gunman.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Fuel costs dominate debate ahead of polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0445e7e755a7bd63d4669b2f0f90640f1d35f9c6a4e830a4069524a41461466</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-fuel-costs-dominate-debate-ahead-of-polls/live-79324526--187ad46b558c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-fuel-costs-dominate-debate-ahead-of-polls/live-79324526?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's coalition government is grappling with record-high fuel prices ahead of two state elections this weekend. Follow DW for more stories making headlines in Germany.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Are food safety rules too much to swallow?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5197017293e9ac3fbe851fe91fa8108626dbf03933c660ab848ca337ffb3e257</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-are-food-safety-rules-too-much-to-swallow/a-79324342--f433b1a7c8ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-are-food-safety-rules-too-much-to-swallow/a-79324342?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent raids at India's luxury hotels and a wider crackdown on its food companies have renewed the debate about food safety standards and their enforcement in the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India heads for driest monsoon in 17 years as El Nino curbs rainfall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8864e2eefe5992840b2446cf7a830e9f9cae1130e7bfe9d636944bb5bb8c98d8</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-heads-for-driest-monsoon-in-17-years-as-el-nino-curbs-rainfall/live-79320496--daae987a1381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-heads-for-driest-monsoon-in-17-years-as-el-nino-curbs-rainfall/live-79320496?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">El Nino has put India on track for its driest monsoon since 2009. Meanwhile, the Election Commission has barred both Trinamool factions from using the party's name in by-elections. More with DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Protests erupt over deaths of 37 miners in custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51e5453003c55e6ef25607ae3cedc1ab1ada3789ab1f0a3061174eace6578d7a</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-protests-erupt-over-deaths-of-37-miners-in-custody/a-79316847--075eb6c61d78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-protests-erupt-over-deaths-of-37-miners-in-custody/a-79316847?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of suspects accused of illegal mining were found dead in custody in Nigeria's north-central Niger State. Officials blame disease, while reports cite overcrowding and poor ventilation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4365181c8e184a739439c8c9632c7a564bf0246f6aaf0bd032b535ef6f432b3e</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35ea53a339f6c2f21ec291983ac35d7aa513ce9117b5bc11557b0d54a3fe1fb7</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bolivia: New cat species discovered by scientists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54a184e17b057bfcc62b98a2fdb771a2f88bd22b06ceb5c72fc7c0e647f338cc</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:02:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bolivia-new-cat-species-discovered-by-scientists/a-79320205--b47b6e8037cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bolivia-new-cat-species-discovered-by-scientists/a-79320205?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Genetic data confirmed that the small feline, called "tilcayo" by locals, is a new species of cat. It's the first such discovery in more than 100 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ce095f539cd15826a605d757bd6d8e32eb9fe7b9506376921ccb5b46478bb81</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Australia: Man killed in shark attack near Perth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b3d891d633e618100cac8ec14dabf74d648277a3f08680627d39eb582d46b8e</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-man-killed-in-shark-attack-near-perth/a-79319936--46c1e6e03276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-man-killed-in-shark-attack-near-perth/a-79319936?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A swimmer was mauled by a shark, with witnesses reporting a massive pool of blood in the water. There have been four confirmed fatal shark attacks in Australia this year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela unblocks some news websites censored for years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0893610242673f7fa580459ea0a9835460cfcc8eed2957334916f88bf29196fe</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuela-unblocks-some-news-websites-censored-for-years/a-79319441--2dcaf370998b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-unblocks-some-news-websites-censored-for-years/a-79319441?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Venezuela has restored access to 17 news sites that were blocked for years under Nicolas Maduro's administration. While activists welcomed the move, they noted that dozens more news portals, remain inaccessible.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia: Jailed ex-leader Najib allowed house arrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2016e4ee732020f602e707c8d5e485c22bdbe0222311327c20cfac46c135813c</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T07:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/malaysia-jailed-ex-leader-najib-allowed-house-arrest/a-79318399--5817740267a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/malaysia-jailed-ex-leader-najib-allowed-house-arrest/a-79318399?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Convicted in the 1MDB scandal for embezzling millions, former Prime Minister Najib Razak had repeatedly sought clemency. Malaysia's king has now granted him a "conditional pardon."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4700a1a12e0a35f2860a8fc0b673646d2b02906c342c737028f65e4418440deb</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Organized crime and drug-related deaths rise Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0797c6b85792f938eb2ef0b6c6b0339007eeb45c994e4ef2328382308aae2702</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/organized-crime-and-drug-related-deaths-rise-germany/a-79315774--74932d6d2d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/organized-crime-and-drug-related-deaths-rise-germany/a-79315774?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Presenting its annual report for organized crime, the German police said that cocaine was a danger for the state and society, and that the cases of money laundering had increased.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russia votes for new parliament in controlled elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fc5693b6765fa2ef7316a926403e8d8d781e53c08332b913e2772485ab99756</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:03:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-votes-for-new-parliament-in-controlled-elections/a-79318392--44a84576087d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-votes-for-new-parliament-in-controlled-elections/a-79318392?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is holding elections for the State Duma for the first time since Moscow sent troops into Ukraine in 2022. The party of President Vladimir Putin is expected to win the highly controlled affair.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Aztec manuscript returns to Mexico after two centuries, on loan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8689ec15de40dc565a0565073a122f551a51d6d37d12bd7c2e9971966b0ac068</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T03:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-after-two-centuries-on-loan/a-79316983--e03b036933bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-after-two-centuries-on-loan/a-79316983?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For years, Mexico has demanded the return of a treasured manuscript. Now the Aztec relic is back home from France — but on loan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN mission notes possible US war crimes in Iran strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:774062e39907f7553bf979eda785282e15731a28326196e896b84743914b3ce9</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T23:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-mission-notes-possible-us-war-crimes-in-iran-strikes/a-79316385--8fe5df816f6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-mission-notes-possible-us-war-crimes-in-iran-strikes/a-79316385?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A United Nations fact-finding mission said it found "reasonable grounds" to believe that the United States committed war crimes in two airstrikes in Iran.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
